This prototype derives isolated functions and CUDA source from SGLang source
captured read-only from image
sha256:614b1509bcb729c653528d448bff9850f8977fcad9d12ba56bd6dbe3d7985e87.
Source project: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
Exact input SHA256 and generated-output SHA256 are in PROVENANCE.json.
The exact image Apache-2.0 LICENSE is retained in LICENSE, SHA256
1495e1e757ef4d0925a2350563cf5754bb23c51701a8ec4fb3c5cdcbedae6747.
Selected original source files contain no license preamble; none was removed.
Changes: active long-path LRU capacity separated from physical Hmax; standalone
MHA dispatch; explicit frozen-policy startup hook. Unrelated upstream methods
are not replaced.

The optional split-copy adapter reuses the existing RecordMissPlan/SkipIO
planner specialization and copy_cache_planned MHA kernel. It adds fixed plan
storage and process-local same-stream routing for validated batch shapes.
The plan/copy kernel mechanism is attributed to SGLang, not claimed as a new
algorithm. The adapter does not enable the upstream side-stream overlap path.

The optional shared-arena resolver (shared_lru_kernel.cuh, shared_lru_device.py)
includes the pinned kvcacheio/hisparse.cuh unmodified for hash_slot and
transfer_item_warp, follows the structure of its block-selection kernel
(short-path and newest-token rules, -1 sentinel, num_real_reqs early exit) and
re-creates the stock MHATokenToKVPool._create_buffers_normal allocation context
(memory-saver region, optional custom pool, identical plane shapes) for one
contiguous allocation. Arena tables, cross-layer victim selection and the
consumer view are new; their pinned inputs are in shared_lru_dependency_sha256.

The optional runtime/compat/minimax_sm80.py is the unchanged experimental BF16
projection adapter used by the existing SM80 launcher, SHA256
207df72e8294982f5153a236043871f38a26b37338c543d9c8322fd56d0c2bf0.
It uses the pinned SGLang MXFP8 dequantization and linear-method interfaces.
It is enabled explicitly and identically for native and arena comparisons.
